item.p:
In the Answer to Request for Arbitration, Respondents request that the Arbitral Tribunal issue an award:58
Respondents’ Answer to Request for Arbitration, ¶ 69.
a.
Declaring that it lacks jurisdiction over any and all claims submitted against Superior Energy; or declaring that claims against Superior Energy are inadmissible pursuant to the terms set forth in the SPA and under Colombian law;
b.
Dismissing all claims asserted in Premium’s Request for Arbitration;
c.
Declaring that Premium and Beneficial Owners breached their obligations under Sections 6(a) and 10.17 of the SPA;
d.
Ordering Premium and Beneficial Owners to compensate Superior Colombia based on the amount resulting from the adjustment of the Purchase Price pursuant to Section 10.17(c)(i) of the SPA;
e.
Ordering Premium and Beneficial Owners to compensate Superior Colombia based on all damages resulting from the breach of their obligations under the SPA and under Colombian law;
f.
Ordering Premium and Beneficial Owners the payment of interest on the sums awarded to Superior Colombia, as applicable;
g.
Ordering Premium and Beneficial Owners to reimburse all costs and expenses incurred by Superior Energy and Superior Colombia in this arbitration, including without limitation all fees and expenses for the arbitrators, the ICC, legal counsel, experts, consultants, witnesses and Superior Energy and Superior Colombia’s own officers and employees;
h.
Awarding to Superior Colombia such other and further relief to which it may show itself to be justly entitled; and
i.
Awarding to Superior Energy such other and further relief to which it may show itself to be justly entitled.

In the Terms of Reference, Respondents request that the Arbitral Tribunal issue an award:59
Terms of Reference, ¶ 91.
a.
Declaring that it lacks jurisdiction over any and all claims submitted against Superior Energy;
b.
If the Tribunal were to find that it has jurisdiction, then declaring that claims against Superior Energy are inadmissible pursuant to the terms set forth in the SPA and under Colombian law;
c.
Dismissing all claims asserted in Premium’s Request for Arbitration;
d.
Declaring that Superior Colombia rightfully withheld the Second Holdback Amount in accordance with the SPA;
e.
Declaring that Premium and Additional Parties breached their obligations under the SPA and Colombian law;
f.
Declaring that Premium and Additional Parties did not comply with or breached the representations and warranties made under the SPA;
g.
Ordering Premium and Additional Parties to compensate Superior Colombia based on the amount resulting from the adjustment of the Purchase Price pursuant to Section 10.17(c) of the SPA;
h.
Ordering Premium and Additional Parties to compensate Superior Colombia based on all damages resulting from the breach of their obligations under the SPA and under Colombian law;
i.
Ordering Premium and Additional Parties to compensate Superior Colombia based on all damages resulting from the non-compliance or breach of the representations and warranties made under the SPA;
j.
Ordering Premium and Additional Parties the payment of interest on the sums awarded to Superior Colombia, as applicable;
k.
Ordering Premium and Additional Parties to reimburse all costs and expenses incurred by Superior Energy and Superior Colombia in this arbitration, including without limitation all fees and expenses for the members of the Tribunal, the ICC, legal counsel, experts, consultants, witnesses and Superior Energy and Superior Colombia’s own officers and employees;
l.
Awarding to Superior Colombia such other and further relief to which it may show itself to be justly entitled; and
m.
Awarding to Superior Energy such other and further relief to which it may show itself to be justly entitled.

In their Memorial of Counterclaims, the Respondents request to the Arbitral Tribunal to render an award:60
Respondents’ Memorial of Counterclaim, ¶ 137.
a.
Declaring that Sellers breached their obligations under the SPA and Colombian law;
b.
Declaring that Sellers did not comply with or breached the representation made under Section 4.14 of the SPA;
c.
Ordering Claimant to compensate Superior Colombia based on the amount resulting from the adjustment of the Purchase Price pursuant to Section 10.17(c) of the SPA;
d.
Ordering Claimant to compensate Superior Colombia based on all damages resulting from the breach of their obligations under the SPA and under Colombian law;
e.
Declaring that Superior Colombia rightfully withheld the Second Holdback Amount in accordance with the SPA;
f.
Ordering Claimant the payment of interest on the sums awarded to Superior Colombia, as applicable; and
g.
Ordering Claimant to reimburse all costs and expenses incurred by Superior Energy and Superior Colombia in this arbitration, including without limitation all fees and expenses for the members of the Tribunal, the ICC, legal counsel, experts, consultants, witnesses and Superior Energy and Superior Colombia’s own officers and employees.

In their Memorial of Answer to the Claim Respondents request that the Tribunal enter an award:61
Respondents’ Memorial of Answer to Claim, ¶ 197.
a.
Declaring that it lacks jurisdiction over any and all claims submitted against Superior Energy;
b.
If the Tribunal were to find that it has jurisdiction over Superior Energy, dismissing that Claims with respect to Superior Energy ate inadmissible pursuant;
c.
Dismissing all claims asserted in the Memorial of Claims;
d.
Declaring that Superior Colombia rightfully withheld Holdback Amount No. 2 in accordance with the SPA and Colombian law;
e.
Declaring that Claimant breached their obligations under the SPA and Colombian law;
f.
Declaring that Claimant did not comply with and/or breached the representations and warranties made under the SPA;
g.
Ordering Claimant to compensate Superior Colombia based on the amount resulting from the adjustment of the Purchase Price pursuant to Section 10.17(c) of the SPA;
h.
Ordering Claimant to compensate Superior Colombia based on all damages resulting from the breach of their obligations under the SPA and under Colombian law;
i.
Ordering Claimant to compensate Superior Colombia based on all damages resulting from the non-compliance or breach of the representations and warranties made under the SPA;
j.
Ordering Claimant the payment of interest on the sums awarded to Superior Colombia, as applicable;
k.
Ordering Claimant to reimburse all costs and expenses incurred by Superior Energy and Superior Colombia in this arbitration, including without limitation all fees and expenses for the members of the Tribunal, the ICC, legal counsel, experts, consultants, witnesses and Superior Energy and Superior Colombia’s own officers and employees; and
l.
Awarding to Superior Colombia and Superior Energy such other and further relief to which it may show itself to be justly entitled.
